[agent] ## Summary
[agent] **Offline feature table — done and verified on the platform.**
[agent] I ingested `data/feature_history.csv` into BigQuery (`${GCP_BQ_DATASET}.feature_history_raw`, 573 rows / 80 accounts) via `bq load`, then did all the compute platform-side in a single BigQuery query:
[agent] - For each `account_id`, selected the most recent revision with `event_time <= 1773478800000` (T) using `ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY account_id ORDER BY event_time DESC)` — revisions after T are excluded from the `WHERE` clause so they cannot influence any score.
[agent] - Scored with `ROUND(1/(1+EXP(-(-0.4331*f1 - 0.4499*f2 + 1.9204*f3 - 0.0086))), 6)`.
[agent] - Materialized the result as feature table **`scores36e30a`** in `GCP_BQ_DATASET` (the dataset that backs the feature store), with record key `account_id` and exactly the columns `account_id, score` — **80 rows, one per account** (scores range 3.99e-4 … 0.999997).
[agent] This is the platform's **offline** store representation and grading can read it back through BigQuery.
[agent] **Online / low-latency serving — blocked by a missing capability in the allowed interface.**
[agent] The GCP "platform" distinguishes offline vs. online via **Vertex AI Feature Store**: a *feature group* (offline, over the BigQuery table) plus a *feature online store* + *feature view* (online, low-latency lookup). Those resources are created with:
[agent] - `gcloud ai feature-groups …`
[agent] - `gcloud ai feature-online-stores …` (and `… feature-views`)
[agent] None of these exist in the **GA `gcloud ai`** surface — the GA group list is only `custom-jobs, endpoints, hp-tuning-jobs, index-endpoints, indexes, model-garden, model-monitoring-jobs, models, operations, persistent-resources, tensorboards, tuning-jobs`, and each feature-store command returns `Invalid choice`. The Vertex AI Feature Store commands live exclusively under the **`gcloud beta ai` / `gcloud alpha ai`** tracks, which are hard-blocked by the environment (`DENIED: … gcloud $track is off-interface`).
[agent] Consequently, I created the feature values as an offline BigQuery feature table (the deliverable's data content, one row per account, correct as-of-T semantics), but I could **not** register it as a Vertex AI feature group with version 1 nor enable online/real-time lookup — the allowed GA `gcloud ai` CLI has no feature-store capability at all, and the only commands that provide it are on the blocked beta/alpha tracks.
[agent] **Missing capability to report:** GA `gcloud ai` (the interface under test) exposes no Vertex AI Feature Store commands (feature groups, feature online stores, feature views), so a feature table with the offline/online distinction and low-latency serving cannot be provisioned through it. This capability is only reachable via `gcloud beta/alpha ai`, which is outside the interface.
